      "kind": "theorem",
      "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.RealDefectRootUnique.actual_unique_positive_real_defect_root",
      "title": "Actual PBPS scalar defect: unique positive real root",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A2",
          "label": "arXiv2609.06905v1 D1 positive-root uniqueness background; scalar antecedent to printed B10 canonical joint root",
          "scope": "Exported real scalar uniqueness and genuine original-input same defect/root only. Printed joint GammaP/ontoM/typed B*B, centered order/inverse/polar/H1/dynamics/main/cost/composition remain separate."
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        "lake build Tests.ProximalBPSRealDefectRootUnique"
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J.",
        "Probability laws, normalized S, stationary disintegration, scalar T and positive D/root are conclusions. Any alternative needs only positivity and SAME-square equality; uniqueness is outside the every-observable energy quantifier.",
        "Finite base E does not imply finite L²; rank-zero E and legal αη=1 are retained."
      ],
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. The laws μ,J,ν are probabilities. There exists a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized density is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)), with Λ.IsCondKernel S and Λ.fst=Λ.snd=ν. There exists a bounded selfadjoint T on the actual real L²(ν) such that for every u, ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere, and ∫Tu dν=∫u dν. Its full scalar defect D=I−T² is positive. There exists a bounded positive REAL Γ with Γ²=D and for EVERY scalar u, ‖Γu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². Probability, kernel, T, D positivity and Γ are conclusions; no supplied CFC/root/commutation or finite-dimensional L² certificate is assumed. For EVERY bounded positive REAL alternative Γprime on this SAME marginal whose square is this SAME D, Γprime=Γ. No energy identity is assumed for an alternative. This uniqueness quantifier lies outside the earlier every-u energy assertion. Printed joint/macro ΓP and B.11 still require SAME onto-M transport and the typed B*B identity, which remain separate.",
      "formula": "D=I-T^2,\\quad\\Gamma\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma^2=D,\\quad\\forall\\Gamma^{\\prime}\\ge0,\\ (\\Gamma^{\\prime})^2=D\\Longrightarrow\\Gamma^{\\prime}=\\Gamma.",
      "boundary": "Exported real scalar uniqueness and genuine original-input same defect/root only. Printed joint GammaP/ontoM/typed B*B, centered order/inverse/polar/H1/dynamics/main/cost/composition remain separate.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Produce the same actual scalar defect and root",
          "text": "The original-input actual positive real root theorem produces probability laws, normalized reflected kernel S at every state, disintegration/stationary marginals, selfadjoint contractive mean-preserving AE scalar T and positive D=I−T². Its produced positive real Γ squares to that same D and has full-domain scalar energy. No object certificate is supplied by the caller.",
          "formula": "D=I-T^2\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma\\ge0,\\quad\\Gamma^2=D,\\quad\\|\\Gamma u\\|^2=\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2.",
          "lean": "RealDefectRoot.actual_positive_real_defect_root; hAll; hD; hΓ; hΓSq; hEnergy"
        },
        {
          "title": "Compare every positive alternative root",
          "text": "Fix ANY bounded positive Γprime with Γprime²=D. Its square equals Γ², so the generic real positive-square uniqueness theorem yields Γprime=Γ. The alternative needs no energy identity. The uniqueness quantifier is outside the earlier every-u energy assertion.",
          "formula": "\\forall\\Gamma^{\\prime}\\ge0,\\quad(\\Gamma^{\\prime})^2=D=\\Gamma^2\\Longrightarrow\\Gamma^{\\prime}=\\Gamma.",
          "lean": "L2RealSquareRootUnique.positive_square_roots_unique; hΓ'Sq.trans hΓSq.symm"
        },
        {
          "title": "Use uniqueness in a genuine actual-input test",
          "text": "The anonymous original-input consumer replaces any positive alternative with the produced root, recovering the full scalar energy and contraction for every u. This supplies the canonical scalar root needed for later SAME onto-M transport. The printed joint ΓP/B*B, centered inverse/polar, dynamics and costs remain separate.",
          "formula": "\\|\\Gamma^{\\prime}u\\|^2=\\|u\\|^2-\\|Tu\\|^2,\\quad\\|\\Gamma^{\\prime}u\\|\\le\\|u\\|.",
          "lean": "Tests.ProximalBPSRealDefectRootUnique anonymous example; hUnique; hEnergy; nlinarith"
        }
      ],
      "lean_statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real Hilbert Borel space with canonical volume, including the explicit rank-zero extension. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let 0<α≤β, and assume α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v. Assume η>0 and βη≤1. Define μ(dx) proportional to exp(−V(x))dx, J as the law of (X,X+√η Z) for independent X∼μ,Z∼N(0,I), ν=J.snd, and Λ as the law of (Y,2X−Y) under J. The laws μ,J,ν are probabilities. There exists a Markov kernel S whose every-state normalized density is S(y)=volume.tilted(x↦−V((y+x)/2)−‖y−x‖²/(8η)), with Λ.IsCondKernel S and Λ.fst=Λ.snd=ν. There exists a bounded selfadjoint T on the actual real L²(ν) such that for every u, ‖Tu‖≤‖u‖, Tu(y)=∫u(x)S(y,dx) ν-almost everywhere, and ∫Tu dν=∫u dν. Its full scalar defect D=I−T² is positive. There exists a bounded positive REAL Γ with Γ²=D and for EVERY scalar u, ‖Γu‖²=‖u‖²−‖Tu‖². Probability, kernel, T, D positivity and Γ are conclusions; no supplied CFC/root/commutation or finite-dimensional L² certificate is assumed. For EVERY bounded positive REAL alternative Γprime on this SAME marginal whose square is this SAME D, Γprime=Γ. No energy identity is assumed for an alternative. This uniqueness quantifier lies outside the earlier every-u energy assertion. Printed joint/macro ΓP and B.11 still require SAME onto-M transport and the typed B*B identity, which remain separate.",
      "lean_proof": "Produce the same actual scalar defect and root; Compare every positive alternative root; Use uniqueness in a genuine actual-input test",
